{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788126660,"nonce":"qMEO7U+93Tod+O7WACNg7s77/v0=","title":"Wave 1 remediation. Depends: 1.1, 1.2, 1.3 (all closed). Gates: nothing formally,","message":"but every later verb inherits these paths.\n\nClose the confirmed defects an independent review found in the wave-1 substrate.\nNone were reachable by the acceptance runs — all three blockers are paths the\nlive tests had no reason to enter. Nothing here requires reverting shipped work.\n\n\n1. **`TimeDriver` state survives a game unload.** `TimeDriver.cs:275` clears\n   `Active` only in `Teardown`; `AgentGameComponent`'s `StartedNewGame`/\n   `LoadedGame` do not. An `advance` in flight when the game returns to the\n   main menu never gets a result file, and on the next load it RESUMES and\n   ticks the new colony to finish the old advance, reporting `ticks_elapsed`\n   and `journal_seq` spanning two games. If no game reloads, every main-thread\n   verb answers `busy` forever. Fix: reset on both lifecycle virtuals and fail\n   the in-flight command with `no-active-game`.\n\n2. **`Runtime.Pending` is never drained at a game boundary.** `GameLoaded()`\n   (`Poller.cs:88`) uses a 5-second heartbeat window, so for up to 5s after\n   unload the poller keeps consuming commands (moving them to `done/`) and\n   queueing them for a main thread that will never run. Zero result files.\n   Same fix site as (1).\n\n3. **The red-error dedupe cap silently disables `halt_on_error`.**\n   `Journal.cs:115` stops emitting after `RedErrorCapPerText + 1`; `TimeDriver`\n   `Notice` only ever sees emitted events. From the 5th occurrence of the same\n   error onward, nothing halts — `advance` returns a clean `reason:\"ticks\"`\n   while the error fires thousands of times. This is the exact failure the\n   standing \"zero red errors\" invariant exists to catch. Fix: put the halt tap\n   upstream of the dedupe. The dedupe policy itself is right for the journal.\n\n\n4. `Poller.WriteResult` builds JSON outside any try (only `AtomicWrite` is\n   guarded) after the result is already dequeued; `MiniJson.AppendString` NREs\n   on null and the `default:` arm calls `value.ToString()` unguarded. A throw\n   loses that result permanently AND aborts the rest of the poller cycle.\n   Wave-2/3 verbs returning Verse objects make this reachable.\n5. `Journal.Flush` dequeues before writing inside `catch {}` — any writer\n   failure discards the line, producing the seq gap JOURNAL.md calls \"an\n   invariant, not a hope\". Peek before write.\n6. Poller cycle order does not establish the \"journal flushed before the\n   result\" invariant it claims: `Flush()` and the `Outgoing` drain read two\n   independent queues, and `ScanInbox` runs before `Flush`, so the `journal`\n   verb is always up to one cycle stale. Correct order: drain Outgoing to a\n   buffer, Flush, write the buffer; and Flush ahead of ScanInbox.\n\n- `AlertScanner.cs:79` calls `alert.Priority` outside the try that guards\n  `alert.Label`; `Priority` is virtual, so a modded alert skips the whole\n  main-thread body for that frame (advance loop and command drain included).\n- `VerbRegistry.cs:95` unchecked `(int)` on a double: `advance {ticks:1e10}`\n  becomes `int.MinValue` and returns a misleading error.\n- `TimeDriver.cs:113` floors `max_tps` at 30, undocumented.\n- `Poller.Sanitize` collapses distinct ids to one result filename.\n- `errorCounts`/`warningsSeen` grow unbounded on unique texts.\n- Journal seq claim and line enqueue are not atomic, so the FILE can show\n  seq 6 before 5 (filters are order-independent; 5.1 assertions would not be).\n\n- The 1.2/1.3 amendments say letters open \"once per FRAME\". In 1.6\n  `LetterStackTick` also calls `OpenAutomaticLetters()` per TICK. Hooking\n  `ReceiveLetter` was correct either way, but the stated reason is half wrong.\n- `AlertsReadoutUpdate` sweeps 1/24 of alerts per frame, so at ~33 ticks/frame\n  during an advance, `until:{alert:…}` can halt 800-2000 ticks late — not \"a\n  frame or two\". Update JOURNAL.md's wording.\n\n- Kill a game mid-`advance` (return to main menu): the in-flight command gets\n  exactly one result file with `no-active-game`, and a subsequent load does NOT\n  resume the old advance.\n- Commands submitted inside the 5s post-unload window each get exactly one\n  result file.\n- `advance {halt_on_error:true}` halts on the 10th occurrence of a repeated\n  identical red error, not just the first four.\n- A verb returning a null string and an arbitrary object still produces exactly\n  one result file.","files":null}]}